00:36:35.690 --> 00:36:39.350
to one of the other pieces
about network automation

00:36:39.350 --> 00:36:43.460
and what is it that
holds people back.

00:36:43.460 --> 00:36:48.470
Network automation is, by its
nature, harder than compute.

00:36:48.470 --> 00:36:50.930
And this is a--

00:36:50.930 --> 00:36:53.990
back up here.

00:36:53.990 --> 00:36:57.800
And that's due to the
fact that the impact

00:36:57.800 --> 00:37:02.480
and the effect of
network automation

00:37:02.480 --> 00:37:04.550
is very different than compute.

00:37:04.550 --> 00:37:07.814
It must be the shark pressing
the button, I don't know.

00:37:07.814 --> 00:37:09.230
If you think about
compute, we got

00:37:09.230 --> 00:37:10.910
really good at doing
compute automation

00:37:10.910 --> 00:37:13.310
because compute is
relatively isolated.

00:37:13.310 --> 00:37:14.900
The challenge is
doing it at scale.

00:37:14.900 --> 00:37:17.570
You've got to be able to do
lots of whatever that automation

00:37:17.570 --> 00:37:19.280
piece is.

00:37:19.280 --> 00:37:22.940
But you're actually only working
on small, reasonably atomic

00:37:22.940 --> 00:37:26.300
pieces of infrastructure
when you actually manage it.

00:37:26.300 --> 00:37:29.000
Network turns that
whole thing on its head.

00:37:29.000 --> 00:37:32.980
Networking automation is much
more complicated, and, I think,

00:37:32.980 --> 00:37:35.810
gets viewed as more
risky because of the fact

00:37:35.810 --> 00:37:38.990
that network
configuration changes,

00:37:38.990 --> 00:37:42.950
much like managing slides,
has a much broader effect.

00:37:42.950 --> 00:37:45.360
You've got-- you make a
network configuration change.

00:37:45.360 --> 00:37:47.776
And there are a whole set of
potentially connected devices

00:37:47.776 --> 00:37:49.180
that are tied to it.

00:37:49.180 --> 00:37:50.930
It means that there's
a lot more perceived

00:37:50.930 --> 00:37:53.450
risk around network automation.

00:37:53.450 --> 00:37:56.590
The real paradox to my
mind is that here you've

00:37:56.590 --> 00:37:58.340
got an environment in
which there is risk,

00:37:58.340 --> 00:38:00.800
but yet there's still
really low automation.

00:38:00.800 --> 00:38:03.710
And automation would get you to
the point at which you actually

00:38:03.710 --> 00:38:06.840
can reduce risk because you're
doing fewer manual operations.

00:38:06.840 --> 00:38:09.410
So it's one of these
crazy situations when we

00:38:09.410 --> 00:38:11.390
think about how you manage it.

00:38:11.390 --> 00:38:13.310
But there's a
significant opportunity

00:38:13.310 --> 00:38:15.440
when you move towards
new environments

00:38:15.440 --> 00:38:18.920
to be able to leverage
native capabilities

00:38:18.920 --> 00:38:23.185
to actually automate away
much of that manual process

00:38:23.185 --> 00:38:24.310
amongst those capabilities.

00:38:24.310 --> 00:38:25.768
LAKSHMI SHARMA: I
think complexity,

00:38:25.768 --> 00:38:29.570
